# Jetpack Compose Components Guide

## Common Components

All reusable Compose components are located in [ui/compose/common/](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ui/compose/common). When creating new UI components:

1. **Buttons**
   - Use [AppBorderButtonComponent.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ui/compose/common/AppBorderButtonComponent.kt) for bordered buttons
   - Follow existing button patterns for consistency

2. **Theme**
   - Colors defined in [Color.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ui/theme/Color.kt)
   - Typography defined in [Type.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ui/theme/Type.kt)
   - Theme configuration in [Theme.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ui/theme/Theme.kt)

## Screen Structure

Each screen should follow this structure:
```kotlin
@Composable
fun ScreenName(
    uiState: UiState,
    onAction: (Action) -> Unit,
    modifier: Modifier = Modifier
) {
    // Screen content
}
```

## UI State Pattern

Each screen should have:
1. A Route file (e.g., `*Route.kt`)
2. A Screen file (e.g., `*Screen.kt`)
3. A UiState file (e.g., `*UiState.kt`)
4. A ViewModel (if needed)

Example implementation in [SignupScreen.kt](app/src/main/java/com/wildflower/mobile/app/ux/startup/auth/signup)

## Best Practices

1. Use composable previews for development
2. Follow material design guidelines
3. Implement proper state hoisting
4. Use remember and derivedStateOf appropriately
5. Implement proper error handling and loading states
6. Use proper spacing and padding constants
7. Follow accessibility guidelines
